1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,440
 Hi, in this lesson, I will talk about prompt engineering basics. Let's get started.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:11,360
 A prompt is simply the text you type to the AI to begin a chat or get a reply.

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,200
 It doesn't have to be text only, it can also be an image or even a sound.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:24,720
 Prompt engineering means writing and adjusting your prompts in a way that makes the AI respond

5
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:30,960
 exactly how you need. It's like given clear directions so you get the best possible result.

6
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:36,560
 When you think about prompt engineering and working with large language models,

7
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:42,400
 it helps to understand how they are built. This models are trained on massive amounts of

8
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:48,080
 text that reflect how people normally talk and write. Because of this, they work best when

9
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:55,520
 your prompts sound like clear, natural requests, just as you would ask another person. For example,

10
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:01,520
 if you tell someone, do this task for me without details, chances are they won't do it the way you

11
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:09,280
 expect. But if you explain clearly what you want step by step, the result will be much closer to your

12
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:16,480
 needs. The same is true for prompt engineering. The clearer and more detailed your instructions are,

13
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:22,000
 the better answers you will receive. Here are some simple rules for good prompting,

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,240
 first always be clear and specific. Tell the AI exactly what you need and give enough details

15
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:34,880
 so it understands. For example, instead of just saying, help me with JavaScript, you could say,

16
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:38,720
 show me how to add two numbers in JavaScript and print the result.

17
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:48,880
 Another example. Instead of explain arrays, try. Explain how to get the first item from

18
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:55,920
 an array in JavaScript. Use a simple example with fruits. Another important rule is garbage in

19
00:01:55,920 --> 00:02:02,320
 garbage out. The quality of the answer depends directly on the quality of your prompt.

20
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:08,560
 If your request is vague or missing details, the response will not be useful.

21
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:14,160
 But if you use clear words, correct details and provide context, such as code snippets,

22
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:19,760
 technical stack, library names or versions, the AI will give you much better results.

23
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:26,960
 For example, instead of saying, fix my code, you could write, fix this JavaScript code.

24
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:32,000
 It should return the correct sum, but right now it gives the wrong result.

25
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:39,840
 And instead of just saying, write unit tests, you might ask, write unit tests for the calculate

26
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:48,000
 discount function. And the project uses TypeScript and YTest. Cover cases for 0%, 10%,

27
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,480
 and 50% discounts. Next, always use good grammar and spelling.

28
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:58,640
 If the AI relies on grammar and spelling to understand your request, if your prompt has too many

29
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:04,800
 mistakes, the result may also be incorrect. Writing correctly gives you more accurate answers.

30
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:12,560
 For example, instead of a Mac just for contention add, name PLS past, write, make a JavaScript

31
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:21,200
 function that adds two numbers. And instead of how just a reward, export, write, explain how race

32
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:27,280
 work in JavaScript with a simple example. Another helpful tip is to keep your prompt short and

33
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:34,480
 simple. Don't add extra words that don't help. A short and clear prompt is often better

34
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:40,080
 than a long one full of unnecessary details. Too much text can confuse the AI.

35
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:47,360
 For example, instead of writing a long paragraph about how you feel stuck in JavaScript,

36
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:54,640
 just ask, show me how to loop through an array in JavaScript. It also helps to give examples.

37
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:00,560
 If you want a specific style of format, show the AI an example in your prompt.

38
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:07,200
 And that way, the AI will follow the pattern. For instance, instead of saying, make a list of

39
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:16,400
 users, you can say, make a list of three users in this format. Name, age, example, Anna, 25.

40
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:24,160
 Or instead of write JavaScript objects for products, try, write two product objects in JavaScript,

41
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:30,240
 provide the expected object format you want to get from AI. When your task feels too big,

42
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:36,560
 it's a good idea to split it into smaller steps. Ask in the AI to handle everything in one go,

43
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:42,400
 often leads to answers that are confusing or not very useful. By breaking things down,

44
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:47,360
 you'll get clear, more focused results, and it'll be easier to learn along the way.

45
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:53,520
 Before. Teach me everything about JavaScript in one answer, including arrays,

46
00:04:53,520 --> 00:05:00,080
 functions, loops, objects, asynchronous code, and advanced topics like promises and classes,

47
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:07,920
 and give me lots of examples for each. After. Explain what a JavaScript function is with one

48
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:15,120
 simple example, and then give. Explain what arrays are and why they are needed with a simple example,

49
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:21,920
 a work step by step. Think of prompting as a back and forth chat, start with a simple request,

50
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:27,680
 with the answer, and then adjust your next prompt. If you don't like the result, change your

51
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:34,960
 wording, add more details, or try another angle. For example, instead of asking for a full online

52
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:42,560
 shop website, all at once, you could first say create a React project using, and then continue with

53
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:48,720
 create a login page with email and password fields, and make it look nice with simple styling.

54
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:56,560
 You can also ask the AI to make a plan. If you don't know where to start, request a roadmap,

55
00:05:56,560 --> 00:06:02,720
 a study plan, or checklist of steps. Once you have the plan, go through each item one by one.

56
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:08,320
 For instance, instead of just saying, teach me JavaScript, you could ask,

57
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:15,600
 make a four-week study plan for learning JavaScript, include weekly goals, topics, and simple

58
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:23,680
 practice tasks. Instead of build me a React app, you might ask, make a step-by-step plan for

59
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:30,080
 building a React app with login, database, and a dashboard, then we'll go through each step in order.

60
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:36,720
 Another powerful tip is to set the tone of the response. You can tell the AI how you want the

61
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:45,600
 answer to sound, friendly, formal, casual, professional, funny, or serious. For example,

62
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:52,400
 instead of asking, explain the difference between const and let JavaScript variables, you might say,

63
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:59,440
 explain the difference between const and let JavaScript variables in a friendly and simple way,

64
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:06,080
 like you're teaching a beginner. Or instead of write project documentation for login feature,

65
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:13,600
 ask, write professional documentation for my project's login feature, use clear sections and bullet

66
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:20,240
 points, prompting us a skill that improves with practice. The clearer and more detailed your input,

67
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:26,480
 the better the answers you will get. You don't need to write the perfect prompt on the first try,

68
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:35,200
 just sync of it as a chat, ask, check and improve. When facing a big task, start by asking the AI

69
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:40,880
 to create a simple plan or roadmap, that structure will make the next steps much easier.

70
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:47,120
 If you follow the simple rules, you'll save time, avoid confusion, and get much more useful

71
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:53,840
 answers from chat GPT. I hope this lesson was useful for you and see you in the next lesson.

